# Requiting Hex chooses its target after its additional cost (blight 1), so it is offered only if its slot could have a
# legal target (CR 601.2c): with nothing on the battlefield but Bot2's Phyrexian Dragon Engine (mana value 3), Bot1 is not
# offered the Hex at all. Once Bot2's Llanowar Elves (mana value 1) is there, it is, and destroys the Elves.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Requiting Hex
Island x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Phyrexian Dragon Engine
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot2.Hand.Phyrexian Dragon Engine.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Requiting Hex.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Requiting Hex.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Emerald; Phyrexian Dragon Engine
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves; Black Lotus
Bot1.Graveyard = Requiting Hex
